@startuml
title FE-09 — Recruiter Reviews, Overrides and Shortlists
skinparam dpi 300
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #CBD5E1
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
hide footbox
autonumber

actor Recruiter
boundary "React Ranking Page" as FE
control "Tenant + JWT Security" as Security
boundary RankingReviewController as Controller
control RankingReviewService as Service
control HumanDecisionPolicy as Policy
control AuditService as Audit
database "Dedicated Tenant DB" as DB

note over Security,DB
Preconditions: Recruiter owns the Job; ranking breakdown is available.
Filters/sorts are read-only UI operations and never alter persisted rank.
end note

Recruiter -> FE: Open candidate breakdown and evidence
FE -> Security: GET /applications/{id}/ranking-review
activate Security
Security -> Security: Validate tenant, role and Job ownership
alt Unauthorized or cross-tenant
  Security --> FE: 403/404 generic response
else Authorized
  Security -> Controller: Forward request
  Controller -> Service: review(applicationId)
  activate Service
  Service -> DB: Read snapshot, sources and active override
  DB --> Service: CandidateRankingDetail
  Service --> Controller: Automated + effective label and reasons
  Controller --> FE: 200 detail
  deactivate Service
  FE --> Recruiter: Explain score, evidence and provenance

  alt Recruiter overrides advisory recommendation
    Recruiter -> FE: Select label and enter mandatory reason
    FE -> Controller: POST /applications/{id}/ranking-overrides
    Controller -> Service: override(actor, id, request)
    activate Service
    Service -> Policy: validate role, reason and expected ranking version
    alt Invalid reason or stale version
      Policy --> Service: Reject
      Service --> Controller: 400 / 409
      Controller --> FE: Explain correction/refresh required
    else Valid override
      Policy --> Service: Allowed
      Service -> DB: BEGIN; append override without changing AI snapshot
      Service -> Audit: record before/after, actor and reason
      Audit -> DB: INSERT immutable audit event
      Service -> DB: COMMIT
      Service --> Controller: Effective recommendation updated
      Controller --> FE: 200 review result
    end
    deactivate Service
  else Recruiter shortlists candidate
    Recruiter -> FE: Confirm shortlist
    FE -> Controller: POST /applications/{id}/shortlist
    Controller -> Service: shortlist(actor, id, request)
    activate Service
    Service -> Policy: requireHumanReview(SHORTLIST, automatedLabel)
    Policy --> Service: Allowed human decision
    Service -> DB: Lock Application; update workflow stage/version
    Service -> Audit: record human shortlist decision
    Audit -> DB: INSERT immutable audit event
    Service -> DB: COMMIT
    Service --> Controller: Shortlisted status
    Controller --> FE: 200 result
    deactivate Service
  end
end
Security -> Security: Clear TenantContext in finally
deactivate Security

note over Policy,DB
Automated NOT_RECOMMENDED never invokes rejection.
Reject is a separate authenticated workflow action with human audit evidence.
end note
@enduml
